{
  "id": "temporal-portal-walk",
  "title": "The first routed temporal frame equals the same walk with spatial rendering",
  "binding": "Both legs run the existing portal-walk world, the identical crossing script and the same Native render tier. Positive enables temporal reconstruction and must count its resolve pass; the off control must have no resolve pass. Both scripts pause the simulation while the engine becomes ready, then resume before the same fixed walk so asynchronous pipeline warmup cannot shift its clock. The existing crossing capture records exactly the first presented destination frame, before another sample can accumulate. Their whole-frame RGB values must agree exactly through the runner-owned opposite-leg image comparison. Existing blue-before, green-after and first-destination-frame observations remain. Replaying the positive activation claim on the off control must fail independently of the pixel equality.",
  "bootShape": "offscreen",
  "backends": [
    "vulkan",
    "directx"
  ],
  "requirements": [
    "gpu"
  ],
  "timeoutSeconds": 60,
